{
  "id": "COMPOUND:23161 - PROTEIN:6147",
  "verbalization": "Dichotomine E is implicated in the activation of the Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9 through multiple pathways, all of which involve the Microtubule-associated protein 1B. This protein serves as a common intermediate in the targeting of the SDR family member 9, with evidence suggesting that Dichotomine E directly interacts with Microtubule-associated protein 1B, which in turn is targeted by various compounds, including Oleamide and 6-Hydroxy-2-[2-(2-hydroxyphenyl) ethyl]chromone. These compounds are all part of a broader class of molecules that modulate the SDR family member 9 through distinct but related mechanisms. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Dichotomine E in influencing the activity of the SDR family member 9 via the Microtubule-associated protein 1B, which may act as a bridge in the signaling or metabolic processes that the SDR family member 9 is involved in. The evidence is consistent with a mechanistic link, though the exact nature of the interaction between Dichotomine E and Microtubule-associated protein 1B remains to be fully elucidated.",
